  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue:
    character: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 96eb344a6948b4d6d9857fbd42887954, type: 3}
    character2: {fileID: -3929998360153519, guid: 7768e6cd5d1d84ba3b1a2c94654bef5d, type: 3}
    name: Liezel
    soundToPlay: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3eb1024c55ce8430ba259a61060f08e3, type: 3}
    audioPitchOffset: 0
    font: {fileID: 0}
    textSpeed: 0.024
    textPunctSpeed: 0.18
    lettersUntilSFX: 3
    sentences:
    - <i>(He speaks of kulonium and the kapisanan as if they are the real enemy.
      What made him oppose them so strongly? Is he only blaming them to protect whatever
      the Disidensya is planning? )</i>
    - <i>(Does he think kulonium will eventually take over Giyala? How is that outcome
      any different from a government that drives its country to chaos in secret?)</i>
    - "Is it not also inhumane to hide from the people one serves? \r"
    - When the majority of people experience inexplicable events, one would rely
      on the highest models of governance...
    - "...and yet we gain no answers\u2014only more questions. There must be information
      that only a strong group of people would know of..."
